<title>MEXICO: Mexico says satellite sale to begin by July.</title>
<headline>Mexico says satellite sale to begin by July.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Companies will be invited to bid in Mexico's satellite privatization in July, Mexico's Communications and Transport Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>Winning bidders will be announced by September or October, deputy communications secretary Javier Lozano said in a press conference.</p>
<p>Up to 75 percent of assets of the nation's three satellites will be sold. The remaining shares will be kept in a government trust and after five years floated on the stock exchange.</p>
<p>Mexico's satellite system generates annual income of almost $110 million.</p>
<p>((--Cyntia Barrera Diaz, Mexico newsroom +525 728 9549))</p>
